            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Symmetry"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.121,
            0.415,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Paper Folding and Cutting"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.149,
            0.633,
            0.17
          ],
          "content": "Here is another way of making symmetric shapes!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.173,
            0.57,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "In these two figures, a sheet of paper is folded and a cut is made along the dotted line shown. Draw a sketch of how the paper will look when unfolded."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.264,
            0.569,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": "Do you see a line of symmetry in this figure? What is it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.583,
            0.186,
            0.822,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.308,
            0.747,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "Make different symmetric shapes by folding and cutting."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.332,
            0.834,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "There are more ways of folding and cutting pieces of paper to get symmetric shapes!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.377,
            0.504,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": "Use thin rectangular coloured paper. Fold it several times and create some intricate patterns by cutting the paper, like the one shown here. Identify the lines of symmetry in the repeating design. Use such decorative paper cut-outs for festive occasions."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.514,
            0.379,
            0.806,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.575,
            0.302,
            0.598
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.606,
            0.325,
            0.625
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Punching Game"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.628,
            0.834,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "The fold is a line of symmetry. Punch holes at different locations of a folded square sheet of paper using a punching machine and create different symmetric patterns."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
